@startuml agent_run_state_machine
!theme plain
title ArthLens System — AgentRun State Machine

skinparam state {
    BackgroundColor White
    BorderColor #2B5797
    ArrowColor #2B5797
}

' Distinct styling for terminal states
skinparam state<<terminal>> {
    BackgroundColor #FBE9E7
    BorderColor #D32F2F
    BorderThickness 2
    FontColor #B71C1C
}

skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FFFDE7
    BorderColor #FBC02D
    FontColor #333333
}

[*] --> CREATED : Run created (POST /runs)\n[Cost & quota reserved at API boundary]

state CREATED {
    CREATED : Initial state upon run instantiation
    CREATED : Budget reserved, parameters validated
}

state INTERPRETING {
    INTERPRETING : Parsing user input and context
    INTERPRETING : Resolving geo units, sector, constraints
}

state PLANNING {
    PLANNING : Generating / updating ActionPlan
    PLANNING : Selecting tools, data providers, models
}

state EXECUTING {
    EXECUTING : Invoking tools and running simulations
    EXECUTING : Registering quantities into Ledger
}

state OBSERVING {
    OBSERVING : Analyzing tool outputs and metrics
    OBSERVING : Checking step completion and errors
}

state RECOVERING {
    RECOVERING : Formulating recovery strategy
    RECOVERING : Bounded retry counter incremented
}

state AWAITING_USER {
    AWAITING_USER : Paused waiting for user input
    AWAITING_USER : Clarification or missing parameters requested
}

state AWAITING_APPROVAL {
    AWAITING_APPROVAL : Paused waiting for explicit user sign-off
    AWAITING_APPROVAL : Gated action encountered
}

state VERIFYING {
    VERIFYING : Running LedgerVerifier (Specifications V1–V9)
    VERIFYING : Gating claims against epistemic rules
}

' Terminal States (4 exact terminal states per Handbook Part 8.2)
state COMPLETED <<terminal>> {
    COMPLETED : All plan goals achieved
    COMPLETED : Verification passed (V1–V9 satisfied)
    COMPLETED : Final Report rendered with chips
}

state FAILED <<terminal>> {
    FAILED : Unrecoverable error encountered
    FAILED : Planning failure or max retries exceeded
}

state BUDGET_EXHAUSTED <<terminal>> {
    BUDGET_EXHAUSTED : Per-run budget limit reached
    BUDGET_EXHAUSTED : Safe partial state persisted in Ledger
}

state CANCELLED <<terminal>> {
    CANCELLED : Gated action rejected by user
    CANCELLED : Execution halted cleanly
}

' ==============================================================================
' TRANSITIONS (Handbook Part 8.2 Authoritative Specification)
' ==============================================================================

' CREATED
CREATED --> INTERPRETING : Start run execution

' INTERPRETING
INTERPRETING --> PLANNING : Intent & parameters understood
INTERPRETING --> AWAITING_USER : Clarification needed

' AWAITING_USER
AWAITING_USER --> PLANNING : User response received

' PLANNING
PLANNING --> EXECUTING : Plan ready
PLANNING --> PLANNING : Re-planning / sub-goal decomposition
PLANNING --> FAILED : Planning failed (unsatisfiable constraints)

' EXECUTING
EXECUTING --> OBSERVING : Execution step completed

' OBSERVING
OBSERVING --> EXECUTING : Continue plan execution
OBSERVING --> RECOVERING : Error or anomaly detected
OBSERVING --> AWAITING_APPROVAL : Gated action encountered
OBSERVING --> VERIFYING : All execution goals met

' AWAITING_APPROVAL (Handbook Part 8.2 exact specification)
AWAITING_APPROVAL --> EXECUTING : Action approved by user
AWAITING_APPROVAL --> CANCELLED : Action rejected by user

' RECOVERING
RECOVERING --> EXECUTING : Retry action directly [retries < max]
RECOVERING --> PLANNING : Re-formulate recovery plan [retries < max]
RECOVERING --> AWAITING_USER : Ask user for guidance
RECOVERING --> FAILED : Recovery limit exceeded [retries >= max] / unrecoverable

' VERIFYING
VERIFYING --> COMPLETED : Verification passed [V1–V9 satisfied]
VERIFYING --> RECOVERING : Verification failed [recoverable violations]

' Budget Exhaustion (Evaluated during run execution from any active state)
INTERPRETING --> BUDGET_EXHAUSTED : Run budget limit hit
PLANNING --> BUDGET_EXHAUSTED : Run budget limit hit
EXECUTING --> BUDGET_EXHAUSTED : Run budget limit hit
OBSERVING --> BUDGET_EXHAUSTED : Run budget limit hit
RECOVERING --> BUDGET_EXHAUSTED : Run budget limit hit
VERIFYING --> BUDGET_EXHAUSTED : Run budget limit hit

' Terminal Exit
COMPLETED --> [*]
FAILED --> [*]
BUDGET_EXHAUSTED --> [*]
CANCELLED --> [*]

' ==============================================================================
' SPECIFICATION NOTES
' ==============================================================================

note right of BUDGET_EXHAUSTED
  <b>Run Budget vs. Daily Quota Separation:</b>
  - <b>Per-Run Cost Cap:</b> Configurable budget for the active run
    (initial default: $0.25; not an immutable universal constant).
    Transition to <b>BUDGET_EXHAUSTED</b> occurs mid-run when this limit is hit.
  - <b>Daily Run Quota (e.g. 50 runs/day):</b> Enforced at the API boundary
    (POST /runs returns HTTP 429). It does <i>NOT</i> trigger an AgentRun state transition.
  - <b>Daily Monetary Cap (P1-6 $5.00/day):</b> Verified at API boundary reservation;
    also reconciled mid-run.
end note

note right of AWAITING_APPROVAL
  <b>Gated Actions & Rejection:</b>
  - Actions with high cost, external impact, or low evidence floors
    pause into AWAITING_APPROVAL.
  - <b>Approved:</b> Resumes execution (-> EXECUTING).
  - <b>Rejected:</b> Transitions to CANCELLED per Handbook Part 8.2.
end note

note right of RECOVERING
  <b>Bounded Recovery:</b>
  - Maximum retry threshold (default: 3) tracked in run state.
  - Exceeding limit forces immediate transition to FAILED.
end note

note bottom of CANCELLED
  <b>Target Specification Note:</b>
  AgentRun 13-state lifecycle follows Handbook Part 8.2 exactly.
  Orchestration execution engine is scheduled for Phase 4.
  All transitions enforce strict state validation; illegal transitions raise domain exceptions.
end note

@enduml
